<resources>
    <color name="serupa_surface_brand">#FFD4304D</color> <!-- Alias. Brand fill: primary buttons, checked boxes, the selected day, a Switch that's on, a Progress bar, with `text-on-brand` (white) on it. Light themes: brand 600 or 700, the lightest with 4.5:1 for white text. Dark themes: the same shade, lightened as far as 3:1 on a raised dark card asks and always a touch, 0.02 of OKLCH lightness, while white text keeps 4.5:1 (blue-600 #2563eb becomes #2b6af2), so a button is the same color in both modes. Yellow is the exception: yellow 500 in light and yellow 400 in dark, under yellow-950 text, since a yellow dark enough for white text reads as brown; Yellow Light's fill takes a `border-brand`. Brand text, links, icons and lines are `text-brand`. More contrast: brand 800 with white text in light, brand 300 with brand-950 text in dark. -->
    <color name="serupa_surface_brand_hover">#FFB42C49</color> <!-- Alias. `surface-brand` under the pointer: one step darker, in light and dark themes alike (a dark theme's is lightened as much as its `surface-brand`). More contrast: brand 900 in light, brand 200 in dark. -->
